<!-- A member of a local cluster pooled and balanced by an edge node (conf/local-cluster/README.md; plans/Edge-Node2.md
    §4.4): every member runs this conf, on one external database, and links to the edge node on its own with the
    pairing's key. The edge node (node_role front_edge, conf/edge/MoquiEdgeConf.xml) pools the members linked for the
    pairing and balances its host names over the live ones, so no load balancer of your own is needed, and the members
    need no open port, port forward or fixed address. It is MoquiLocalConf.xml's cluster with the edge node in the load
    balancer's place; what differs is said here. Use the Enterprise package (--enterprise), as for any cluster. -->
<moqui-conf xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/moqui-conf-3.xsd">
    <default-property name="instance_purpose" value="production"/>

    <!-- The shared database, as in MoquiLocalConf.xml: Postgres (or MySQL with the default cluster transport), its
        settings in .env, the same on every member: entity_ds_host, entity_ds_port, entity_ds_database, entity_ds_user,
        entity_ds_password, and entity_ds_sslmode and entity_ds_sslrootcert for its TLS. Back it up with its own tools:
        the backup job covers an embedded database only. -->
    <default-property name="entity_ds_db_conf" value="postgres"/>

    <!-- The same secrets on every member, as in MoquiLocalConf.xml: session_cookie_key, cluster_tls_cert,
        cluster_tls_key and entity_ds_crypt_pass, which the first member's first start generates into its .env.
        The pairing is the cluster's, made once on one member (System › Edge Node, Pair with an edge node), which writes
        edge_node_url, edge_node_key (the pairing's key), edge_node_pin, edge_node_id and edge_node_pairing (the id the
        edge node knows the cluster by, which keys the outbox and its receipts) to that member's .env. Copy that whole
        .env to every other member (the secrets above, the pairing's lines, and the rest that must match, such as
        acme_account_key, ssh_host_key and git_lfs_token_key), then add the member's own cluster_base_url; each links at
        its next start.
        Each member's own: its instance id (runtime/db/instance_id) and its member key (runtime/db/edge_member_key, made
        at its first link), which the edge node pins for its id. Never copy runtime/db between members. A member made
        again with a new key is refused as another node until its key is forgotten on the edge node (System › Edge
        Clients › Clients, Forget key).
        Per member in .env: cluster_base_url, https://(this member's private address):8444, which the other members
        reach. Open 8444 between the members only. -->

    <!-- Admission (plans/Edge-Node2.md §4.4): while a member is linked, a new one is admitted only when a linked
        member's cluster lists it as live, so a member joins the cluster first (its heartbeat in the shared
        database), then links. Anything else with the key, such as a staging copy on another database, is refused "join
        the cluster first" and shows on the edge node's Edge Clients › Clients. With none linked the key admits, which
        is how the pool starts. -->

    <!-- How peers reach this member, as in MoquiLocalConf.xml: empty for its cluster port (TLS with the cluster
        certificate, client certificate required), notify for Postgres LISTEN/NOTIFY on the shared database when members
        cannot connect to each other (Postgres only), ssh through its SSH server (ssh_port; a build with the ssh
        feature). cluster_protocol: empty or grpc for gRPC on HTTP/2, rest for HTTP/1.1 only; members on different
        settings or builds still reach each other. -->
    <default-property name="cluster_transport" value=""/>
    <default-property name="cluster_protocol" value=""/>

    <!-- Web access through the edge node: the client's address comes over the link, so no webapp_trusted_proxies or
        webapp_client_ip_header; each member's web protection counts by it. A passthrough name ends its TLS on the
        member, so each member needs the certificate in runtime/cert (the same files on each); a terminate name ends on
        the edge node and needs none here.
        Balancing (on the edge node): web requests to a terminate name by request, sticky by the session cookie (the
        name per host on Edge Clients › Domains, moqui.session by default), so a client stays on one member and moves,
        still signed in, when that member stops; passthrough names and tunnels by connection, sticky by the client's
        address; delegated calls by conversation; queue items one at a time per key from every linked member. Sessions
        are rows in the shared database, so the session-config flush="guarantee" of MoquiLocalConf.xml is not needed.
        Work from the pool (docs/Run-Deploy.md, Cluster, What is shared and what is not): any linked member sends from
        the outbox, the items of a key in order, each once; one member sends replication and keeps the edge node's call
        media and SIP rows, the one holding the lock row EdgeSenderLock, and the others pass it their change notes on a
        cluster topic. Web protection's bans are shared with the other members and told up the link to the edge node,
        which refuses that client for this pairing's names. -->

    <!-- Draining (plans/Edge-Node2.md §4.4): before stopping or upgrading a member, drain it in its own System › Edge
        Node (This node's cluster, Drain this node), or on the edge node's Edge Clients › Clients: it finishes what it
        has and the edge node sends it no new work, and its /health answers 503. A member says on its links when it is
        starting or stopping, so a rolling upgrade needs nothing more: drain, stop, upgrade, start, resume. Draining the
        only live member takes the pairing's names offline at the edge node until it resumes. -->

    <entity-facade crypt-pass="${entity_ds_crypt_pass}" query-stats="true"/>
</moqui-conf>
